The shoemaker and his wife had one child, whose name was Leo. Leo swept the shop, and sorted the nails, and loved to sit by the bench and watch the leather being cut.

@shoemaker: One evening, about Christmas-time, as he and his wife were sitting over the fire chatting together, he said to her, “I should like to sit up and watch tonight, that we may see who it is that comes and does my work for me.” The wife liked the thought, and Leo begged to stay up too; so they left a light burning, and all three of them hid themselves in a corner of the room, behind a curtain that was hung up there, and watched what would happen.

[bed music music_box tune=lullaby tempo=70 vol=-17 fade=4 duck=6]
[sfx chime count=12 pitch=220 interval=1.2 room=room vol=-18 wait=1]
